   "note": "The task is graph connectivity, which is invariant under node relabeling (S6 symmetry). The previous best proposal (c003) had a single generator hypothesis but used a mix of CRX/CRY/CRZ gates which are less symmetric and harder to train. This proposal uses a highly structured 'Hardware Efficient' style block with uniform RZ rotations, a ring of CZ entanglers, and uniform RX rotations. The CZ ring topology is invariant under cyclic permutations and reflections of the nodes (D6 subgroup of S6). The uniform single-qubit rotations preserve this symmetry if parameters are tied or if the readout averages them, but here we use distinct parameters to allow breaking symmetry if needed for specific graph structures, while the structural bias towards connectivity patterns (via the ring) aligns with the problem's geometric nature. The block is compact (18 gates) to reduce overfitting risk while maintaining sufficient expressivity for connectivity detection.",
